{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510691-vampiric-pallor-and-a-possible-alternative-spin-on-the-assamite-weakness","id":1510691,"title":"Vampiric pallor and a possible alternative spin on the Assamite weakness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-04T03:05:18-07:00","id":1510691,"title":"Vampiric pallor and a possible alternative spin on the Assamite weakness","content":"Possibly a silly idea, but:<br /> Vampires are supposed to get paler with age. Unless they're a Child of Haqim, in which case they're supposed to get more melanin over time. <br /> But vampires always look exactly like they did the day they died. So vampires losing melanin seems contradictory, and vampires not changing skin tone but rather growing pallid from lack of blood circulation seems more apt.<br /> <br /> Which then got me thinking that in that case, the opposite happening to the Assamites would be ruddiness.<br /> <br /> The canon situation of getting a tan and looking like a drow cosplayer in your elder years doesn't work for me. I'm pretty sure I recall there was some piece of folklore that explains why, but it's still meh to me. <span style=\"font-size:9px\">&quot;Oh no, I'm going to get <i>a tan</i>!&quot; To which the Nosferatu would ask you to cry them a fucking river.</span><br /> <br /> So, alternative interpretation: most vampires look increasingly bloodless with time, Assamites look more and more like they're full of blood. Starting with unusually flushed cheeks as a neonate. <br /> I'd take the &quot;vampires cry, come and sweat blood&quot; and apply that specifically to Assamites. Over time all fluids are replaced with blood. Eyes grow redder, ruddy skin starts to look like it's covered in red bruises that get darker with time. They look like their blood vessels have ruptured. You know when there's so much blood it's red-black? <br /> <br /> Earlier in life you have a complexion and you'll soon start a growing collection of &quot;bruises&quot; where blood vessels are close to the skin. By the ancilla stage you're not a guaranteed Masquerade breach, but you do look like you need medical help. Elders are saturated with blood. Methuselahs look like they've gorged themselves on the blood of entire nations in the last five minutes. <br /> <br /> And then the other clans tell their childer about the cult of ravenous cannibal assassins who at all times are barely holding themselves back from consuming your blood and soul, and they can point to the blood gorged monstrosity in the corner: just look at it!<br /> (&quot;And this,&quot; the Tremere can say. &quot;Is one of many reasons why we are invaluable and you're not going to try and kill us all off.&quot;)<br /> <br /> (And then the Viziers and Sorcerers get irritated about being lumped in with the Web of Knives' diablerie nut reputation. They don't even <i>have</i> that curse!)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T04:03:07-07:00","id":1510692,"title":"","content":"Assamite darkening is in line with arsenic poisoning, which makes sense for the assassin clan known for poison. They actually go grey first rather than anything to do with melanin. Also the Darkening gives them a whole &quot;chosen race of authority figures&quot;/diablerie loving devils thing to them which works great for them. It's makes them interesting to have a feature that's designed to set them apart from every other vampire, especially considering their bitter history and how they're their own independent sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T11:23:10-07:00","id":1510897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510691-vampiric-pallor-and-a-possible-alternative-spin-on-the-assamite-weakness?p=1510692#post1510692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They actually go grey first rather than anything to do with melanin.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just worsens my mental image of drow cosplay vampires. No big deal, just a me problem, I guess.<br /> I mean, looking like a walking void of utter darkness <i>is</i> cool, but it takes centuries to actually look that cool and in the meantime...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T12:25:24-07:00","id":1510905,"title":"","content":"Well your hair and eye colour would be unaffected, and you're not gaining pointy ears, so you're not really that far into drow territory. There are IRL people out there with charcoal coloured skin, I think it looks great. Fortunately for formerly-white Assamites, there are ethnicities capable of these skin tones with facial structures more similar to Europeans or west Asians (such as those from southern India) so blackface accusations aren't inevitable. (also, like, obfuscate's a thing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T21:55:50-07:00","id":1510956,"title":"","content":"The original idea seemed to be that Assamites committed so much diablerie that the blackness in their auras bled into their flesh. I'm not sure it still fits a clan that is tempted by diablerie, but doesn't actually commit it much more often than anyone else, as doing so would provoke their genocide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}